#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186353481 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abaeea03-6a2a-5d37-a2af-a9ea109175ad" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reasons Why a Determinant Equals Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59d1c04c-0655-5278-b4c8-f5cb122256d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the statements are true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353483} {:answer/id #uuid "effe2664-62ee-5dbb-9fad-9f920f43a98a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353484} {:answer/id #uuid "10a31744-69eb-5b1f-a777-17f89a385509" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353485} {:answer/id #uuid "e8fdd561-5d2f-51af-8f35-589a4719773a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353486} {:answer/id #uuid "8deac381-da13-59ac-a58c-9fe7d86b3665" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353487}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "effe2664-62ee-5dbb-9fad-9f920f43a98a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353484} :answer-field/id #uuid "bed80140-001f-57ad-baa2-83f36a11c8f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353482}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0fee5ebf-ea7a-5f52-b051-47b6eb42b4bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-140049" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix such that $|A|\\ne 0.$ Which of the following statements must be true?\n\n- $A$ is a triangular matrix\n- $A$ does not have identical rows\n- $A$ does not have proportional columns" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example, consider the matrix \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe have that \n\n$$\n|A|=1\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot 2=5\\ne 0\n$$\n\nbut $A$ is not a triangular matrix.\n\n- Statements II and III are true. Indeed, we can make use of the following fact:\n\n$|A|=0$ *if and only if one of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A.$*\n\nIn the case of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, this means that one of the rows/columns must be proportional to another row/column.\nHence, if $|A|\\ne 0$ then $A$ doesn't have proportional nor identical rows/columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186353488 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abaeea03-6a2a-5d37-a2af-a9ea109175ad" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reasons Why a Determinant Equals Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1764cc7-05e9-5112-8ee0-9aa7445ec1fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353490} {:answer/id #uuid "113e631f-9931-5dae-b17b-bdbb89ead1a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353491} {:answer/id #uuid "22ba1859-a833-508b-9e11-b104d4b330e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353492} {:answer/id #uuid "c714bd58-c00c-5896-8e13-ce699666f697" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353493} {:answer/id #uuid "40d1d860-6eb3-5be7-b31f-c9725452a495" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353494}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "113e631f-9931-5dae-b17b-bdbb89ead1a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353491} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec31cd9b-d080-59fd-986f-e3b1cd80ec12" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353489}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b4149f8e-ec30-57f2-974d-a0f7b6fea8c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-42465" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 8 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & \\sqrt{6} & 9 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 4 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n\n- $A$ has proportional rows\n- $A$ has identical columns\n- $A$ has a zero column" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ has proportional rows: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 8 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & \\sqrt{6} & 9 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 4 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical columns.\n\n- $A$ does *not* have a zero column.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186353495 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abaeea03-6a2a-5d37-a2af-a9ea109175ad" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reasons Why a Determinant Equals Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64a290c0-3cb9-5ab3-86dd-08cb35f733b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353497} {:answer/id #uuid "fc579fde-ef6c-5f8e-833e-84d13352f5af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353498} {:answer/id #uuid "7b4901e2-7aef-5e71-8f47-fa4534a88bdd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353499} {:answer/id #uuid "3c9f3892-7b72-5c10-b490-a230a83a9039" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353500} {:answer/id #uuid "eb230c19-5286-594a-9b0e-149d1cd7d324" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353501}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64a290c0-3cb9-5ab3-86dd-08cb35f733b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353497} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e96eb04-97e5-576e-98df-57805b3bc721" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353496}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "574569eb-6eb7-5fa5-8d63-5857a9ceeeb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-42957" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 10 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n\n- $A$ has identical columns\n- $A$ has a zero column\n- $A$ has identical rows" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical columns.\n\n- $A$ has a zero column: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 10 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\n- $A$ has identical rows: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 10 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186353502 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8aef330a-81b3-56c4-9559-67df673e8687" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Matrix With Two Proportional Rows/Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60ccb0c7-831b-5ba6-a0e6-a1619a95ff3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353504} {:answer/id #uuid "423815c9-7bb5-5bad-8cd3-b9299c91eda6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353505} {:answer/id #uuid "285f48c7-09fa-5df0-9c18-6b8bfd08be8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353506} {:answer/id #uuid "847962f6-fa81-5c02-a37e-f6498e8874f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353507} {:answer/id #uuid "9c6e268b-7e84-5c84-bc3c-106139ca1828" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353508}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60ccb0c7-831b-5ba6-a0e6-a1619a95ff3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353504} :answer-field/id #uuid "7333e439-36d5-5cde-9fc3-f7a8f836a289" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353503}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b44f28c6-ca93-5246-be2b-1a2725d36e07" :question/math-academy-id "q-43057" :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & -6 & 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 8 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4 \\\\ 2 & 2\\sqrt{2} & 8 \\\\ 0 & -\\sqrt{3} & 4\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\sqrt{3} & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is a triangular matrix, hence \n\n$$\n|A|=3\\cdot (-6)\\cdot 2=-36\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has proportional rows: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4 \\\\ 2 & 2\\sqrt{2} & 8 \\\\ 0 & -\\sqrt{3} & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is a triangular matrix, hence \n\n$$\n|C|=(-1)\\cdot 3\\cdot 4=-12\\ne 0\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $|B|$ is equal to $0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186353509 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8aef330a-81b3-56c4-9559-67df673e8687" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Matrix With Two Proportional Rows/Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf651496-8b45-544a-80a4-70cb95dd0be8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353511} {:answer/id #uuid "09d4c143-b82d-5502-b98d-af3d3cd26e1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|B|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353512} {:answer/id #uuid "6876b54f-1039-5bd5-a1f8-ee3e90e109f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353513} {:answer/id #uuid "61ec4819-22a1-5aa1-8eb9-9a818621a288" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353514} {:answer/id #uuid "b8010981-893f-5977-b870-0a27dca1a63e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353515}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09d4c143-b82d-5502-b98d-af3d3cd26e1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|B|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353512} :answer-field/id #uuid "7460ff43-0dca-59fb-a5f4-1b924dd4abe5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353510}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d38fcef1-b0ad-5be5-8eb8-267ed617aedf" :question/math-academy-id "q-82289" :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -8\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{5} & -2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is a diagonal matrix, hence \n\n$$\n|A|=4\\cdot (-2)\\cdot 3=-24\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has a zero column: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -8\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has proportional columns: \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{5} & -2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|C|=0.$\n\nTherefore, only $|B|$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$"}]}
